  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The amplitude of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is modulated by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></math> signal. The amplitude modulated signal contains frequencies of</p><p>A. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p>B. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p>C. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p>D. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>498</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p>E. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>502</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math></p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "xVQNM",
      "text": "A and B only",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "cz0C8",
      "text": "A and C only",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "fUa2H",
      "text": "A and D only",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "CNoSU",
      "text": "A, D and E only",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The carrier wave frequency is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mn>1000</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>The modulating&nbsp;wave frequency is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Hence, the frequencies contained in the modulated signal are given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnspacing=\"0px\" columnalign=\"right center left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>f</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd/><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>498</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>502</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
